values ('f1a2b3c4-5d6e-4f08-9b88-8c9d0e1f2a08', 'ensemble-participation', 'Ensemble Participation', 'Ensemble Participation is a recurring undergraduate music requirement in which students perform in choir, orchestra, band, jazz, chamber, or other approved ensembles. The course develops musicianship through rehearsal discipline, listening, stylistic preparation, conductor response, peer collaboration, and public performance. This course trains students to function as prepared, responsive, and ethical ensemble musicians who can tune, blend, read, lead, follow, rehearse independently, perform across styles, and reflect on their growth.');

